      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "CANYA GURU (1) had the drop on the pace early but forged to the lead on the bend and drew clear to score (17.09) at this track in a Grade 6 over 300m. Has a strong record out of this box with two wins and a minor placing from four starts. In sparkling form and looks the one to beat again. TERRIFIC SHAZAR (8) did a good job to finish third last time out over 395m at this track (22.97) in a Grade 6, the second top-three finish on the trot. Solid beginner and with a good start should have clear running out wide. Can find the frame this time. DASHING STEVE (2) is worth forgiving last start after finishing fifth (20.19) in a Grade 6 at Angle Park over 342m. Has ability and can measure up. ROCK IT RONNIE (6) warrants respect following a recent placing.",
